## Why This Is Asked
This probes data-centric NLP, calibration, and ops in multilingual, low-latency contexts.

## Key Concepts
- Language-aware calibration and conformal prediction
- On-device adapters for multilingual models
- Drift detection and rollback automation
- Canary rollout and per-language metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple temperature scaling for probability calibration (pseudo)
function scale(probs, T){
  const scaled = probs.map(p => Math.pow(p, 1/T));
  const s = scaled.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  return scaled.map(v => v/s);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you set per-language thresholds for rollback?
- What metrics would you monitor for drift and miscalibration?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to enable rapid domain adaptation with privacy guarantees in a real-time environment, emphasizing latency constraints, privacy preservation, and robust rollback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- Parameter-efficient adapters (LoRA/Adapters) for domain adaptation
- On-device fine-tuning with privacy guarantees (DP or federated learning)
- Streaming drift detection and safe rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load base model, attach adapter for domain, fine-tune on small labeled set
function adaptDomain(model, domain, labeledData) {
  const adapter = new LoRAAdapter(model, { rank: 4, alpha: 8 });
  adapter.fineTune(labeledData, { privacy: 'DP-SGD', epochs: 3 });
  return adapter;
}
```

